  "final_answer": "I have found and read the article. Let me provide my findings.\n\n## Task Complete ✅\n\n**Today's date:** September 24, 2026\n\n### Article Found (Published within the last 2 days):\n\n**Title:** \"More than 170,000 respiratory cases recorded in haze-choked Indonesia\"\n\n**Author:** Kelly Ng\n\n**Date Published:** 2 days ago (September 22, 2026) ✅ *Within the last 2 days*\n\n### Article Summary — Environmental Impacts of Deforestation:\n\nThe article documents severe environmental and health impacts caused by wildfires and deforestation in Indonesia:\n\n1. **Public health crisis:** Since August, approximately **175,000 people in Indonesia have suffered from respiratory illnesses** due to toxic smog. More than **40,000 of these cases involve toddlers**, ranging from mild coughs to bronchitis and pneumonia.\n\n2. **Regional air pollution:** Forest fires have blanketed Indonesia, Malaysia, and Singapore in toxic haze, with air quality indices reaching \"unhealthy\" levels.\n\n3. **Worsened by climate conditions:** The 2026 wildfire season has been \"turbocharged\" by a so-called **\"Godzilla\" El Niño**, fueling extremely dry conditions during Indonesia's annual dry season (July–October).\n\n4. **Scale of destruction:** The independent forest monitoring platform **Nusantara Atlas** detected around **734,000 fire hotspots** across Indonesia — a figure more than 30% higher than in 2019, one of Indonesia's worst wildfire seasons. Since January, at least **895,657 hectares** of land (nearly six times the size of Greater London) have been burned.\n\n5. **Response and impact:** Indonesia deployed **54,000+ officials and dozens of aircraft** for water-bombing operations in Borneo and Sumatra. The wildfires led to **school closures** and a surge in **hospital admissions**. The toxic smog has also taken a toll on wildlife, including endangered orangutans in Borneo.\n\nThe article was accessed via BBC News → Earth → \"How toxic smog from wildfires is making Indonesians sick\" video segment → \"More on this story\" link, and directly discusses the environmental consequences of forest fires linked to deforestation in Indonesia.",
